3. Construct the query string \( y = 0^{q(n + \log k)} 1^i 0^{r(n)} x \).
4. Query the oracle \( S \) to check if \( y \in S \).
5. Accept if \( y \in S \); otherwise, reject.

This algorithm respects the format of strings in \( S \), ensuring \( M \) runs in polynomial time.

